id: pm-hiqlkh
title: "GH-1137: linked docs writes silently persist nonexistent workspace paths"
description: "Track GitHub issue #1137: `pm docs <id> --add` accepts and persists a local project path that does not exist, reports success, and leaves validation to a separate opt-in read. The durable dangling link then contaminates future agent context and is absent from the default health signal."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,context-integrity,docs,github,linked-resources
created_at: "2026-08-28T14:42:57.920Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T20:44:39.545Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "Promote path validation policy to the public SDK; return structured existing/missing/remote counts on files and docs writes; support warn and strict modes while preserving explicit forward references; include dangling linked resources in health; add CLI, SDK, MCP, history, config, and temp-workspace acceptance coverage."
parent: pm-33cw
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issue #1137
severity: medium
environment: "pm 2026.8.28, Linux; repository-backed tracker with a nonexistent project-relative docs path"
repro_steps: "Run `pm docs <id> --add path=test/nonexistent-linked-doc.ts,note=planned coverage`; observe changed true, then run `pm docs <id> --validate-paths` to reveal the dangling path."
expected_result: Linked-resource writes make path existence visible at mutation time and expose repository-configurable strict refusal plus fleet-wide health detection without prohibiting explicit forward references.
actual_result: "The write succeeds silently, the nonexistent path persists in the item and history, and only a separate opt-in validation call reveals it."
affected_version: 2026.8.21-2026.8.28
component: linked-resources
regression: false
customer_impact: Agents persist false documentation provenance that is repeatedly returned as context and cannot be distinguished from a real linked resource by later readers.
